pkgfilecache Changes
=====================


Version 0.4.0 -- Declarative file manifests
---------------------------------------------
- NEW: Describe the optional data files of your package in a single declarative manifest (one row per file) instead of three parallel vectors (relative filenames, urls, md5 sums). A manifest is either a CSV file shipped with your package or a data.frame, with columns 'path' (required), and 'url' and 'md5' (both optional). This reduces the friction of adding many files to a package.
- NEW: 'ensure_files_available_from_manifest' is a new entry point like 'ensure_files_available', but it takes a manifest instead of three parallel vectors. The download URL for a file can be derived automatically from a base URL (argument 'base_url') and the manifest path, which is convenient when the remote directory layout mirrors the layout inside the package cache.
- NEW: 'read_manifest' reads a manifest from a CSV file (comment lines starting with '#' are ignored) or accepts a data.frame, validates it and derives missing URLs.
- NEW: 'write_manifest_from_dir' generates a manifest (CSV file) from a local directory, computing the MD5 checksum of every file automatically. Put your files into a directory, run this function once, and add the resulting CSV to your package.
- DEV: Regenerate documentation with roxygen2 8.0.0 (updated 'Config/roxygen2/version' in DESCRIPTION).


Version 0.3.0 -- Parallel Downloads
------------------------------------
- NEW: Parallel downloads: the new 'num_connections' argument of 'ensure_files_available' (default 2) downloads several files at the same time using the 'curl' multi interface, which speeds up downloading many small files. Use num_connections=1 for strictly sequential downloads. Controlling the number of default parallel downloads is also possible via `options` (use `pkgfilecache.num_connections`), allowing the user in an interactive session to control downloads in package code (unless the package author explicitely specified them).


Version 0.2.0 -- Adjust default download dir, support tempdir, maintenance
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
- FIX: Replace the archived 'downloader' package with the modern 'curl' package for all file downloads. 'downloader' is no longer on CRAN.
- DEV: Add a test that downloads and MD5-verifies the same set of (binary, HTTP) data files used by the 'brainloc' package, so such platform-specific download issues are caught on CI, including macOS.
- FIX: Add the package version, not the R-version, to constructed path
- NEW: Use the `tools::R_user_dir` directory as the default package cache location on R 4.0 or later (the location recommended by the CRAN repository policy for user-specific data and cache files), with the legacy `rappdirs` location used as fallback on older R versions. If a cache from an older version of this package already exists at the legacy location, it is reused to avoid re-downloading all files.
- NEW: Allow overriding the package cache location with the R options `pkgfilecache.cachedir` (set a custom cache root directory) and `pkgfilecache.use_tempdir` (redirect the cache to the R session's temporary directory, `tempdir()`). The latter is useful for unit tests and CI systems that must not write to the user's home directory.
- DEV: Run the package's own tests against the R session's temporary directory (via the `pkgfilecache.use_tempdir` option), so the tests never write to the user's home directory, e.g., during CRAN checks.


Version 0.1.5 -- curl and better docs
--------------------------------------
- Add curl as dependency (used in some tests)
- Fix some very minor documentation errors in internal function (CRAN team requested it)


Version 0.1.4 -- Improvements for CRAN
---------------------------------------
- Disable all unit tests that require downloaded data on CRAN
- Use the same name for the vignette title and the vignette index entry
Note: This release contains no feature changes for package users, it was required for technical reasons related to CRAN.


Version 0.1.3 -- Improvements for CRAN
----------------------------------------
- Delete test data after tests on CRAN
Note: This release contains no feature changes for package users, it was required for technical reasons related to CRAN.


Version 0.1.2 -- Bug fixes and better docs
------------------------------------------
- Fix bug in accessing files in local sub directories of the package cache
- Document how to download files to a local subdir in the vignette
- Document how to access files in local subdir in the vignette
- Adapt tests to make package build for MacOS on CRAN


Version 0.1.1 -- Subdir support
---------------------------------
- Added support for storing files in sub directories in the local file cache


Version 0.1.0 -- Initial Release
----------------------------------
- Initial release
